Third-party test data for pubrs (`tests/corpus/pub/`)

This directory holds Microsoft Publisher files and reference data used to test
the `.pub` importer. The files are test inputs only; none is linked into or
shipped with pubrs.

1. poi/  (24 files: .pub documents and the Sample*.txt text extractions)
   Source:   Apache POI, test-data/publisher
             https://github.com/apache/poi
   Commit:   ae62bb5116b9aee19ebd5834e3a82066132c9f7f (ae62bb51)
   Licence:  Apache License 2.0
             Full text: LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt (next to this file)
   Copyright (c) The Apache Software Foundation. The files are unmodified.

2. libreoffice/  (4 .pub files)
   Source:   LibreOffice core, writerperfect/qa/unit/data/draw/libmspub/pass
             https://github.com/LibreOffice/core
   Commit:   63a2e19 (see libreoffice/COMMIT for the full hash)
   Licence:  Mozilla Public License 2.0
             Full text: LICENSE-MPL-2.0.txt (next to this file)
   The files are unmodified. Three of them (EDB-*) are crafted exploit samples
   that exist to check that importers fail safely.

3. expected.json and oracle/text/
   Generated for pubrs from the files above by converting each with LibreOffice
   25.2.3.2 (libmspub 0.1.4) to PDF and reading the result with poppler: page
   count, page size, image count, word count and the extracted text. LibreOffice
   and libmspub are used as a reference tool only; their output text is the text
   of the Publisher files above.

The SHA-256 of every file here is in SHA256SUMS. ASSETS.md at the repository
root lists these sources.
